## Accessibility (target WCAG 2.2 AA)

Quick reference: https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/

### Perceivable

- Meaningful alt text; decorative images `alt=""`
- Icons and icon-only controls have accessible names
- Contrast 4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large text; status not color-only
- Logical heading order; tables with headers

### Operable

- Full keyboard access; visible focus; logical tab order; no traps
- Modals: focus moves in, returns to trigger on close (`ModalForm` handles common cases)

### Understandable

- Labels on inputs; required fields indicated; errors described with recovery steps

### Robust

- Prefer semantic HTML; ARIA only when semantics insufficient; live regions for dynamic status

### PF-specific

- PatternFly accessibility (develop): https://www.patternfly.org/accessibility/develop/
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — prefer PF/CSS on transform/opacity; avoid animating height/margin for layout

---

## User experience states

**Loading:** `LoadingSuspend`, spinners, skeletons where appropriate  
**Empty:** `EmptyState` with next-step guidance  
**Error:** Alerts with actionable copy; preserve user input where possible  
**Long operations:** Migration/progress — non-blocking alerts, clear status in tables  

