## Modes of work

### Design-phase mode (dev-helper or *"design layout"*)

Produce a **Structural layout** section (and optional expanded `layout-plan.md` for complicated/complex UI). Use this template:

```markdown
## Structural layout

**Screen type:** list | details | wizard | modal | inline panel | other

**Reference screens in plugin:** (paths)

**Component tree:** (PF component names; mermaid or indented list)

**Regions:** title, alerts, toolbar, main, side panel, footer actions

**Primary / secondary actions:**

**Navigation & wayfinding:** tabs, breadcrumbs, links

**States by region:** loading | empty | error | success | partial

**Content notes:** labels, helper text, error copy (i18n keys)

**A11y notes:** focus order, modal trap, live regions, keyboard path
```

### Review-phase mode (code or mockup review)

Use the **output format** below. Each finding uses a severity prefix (🔴 blocker,
🟡 suggestion, 🟢 enhancement, ✅ positive) — do not add a separate severity field.
Cite **analogous MTV page** from `forklift-ux-patterns.mdc`. Flag PF composition
issues separately from a11y.

---

## Review checklist

- [ ] Keyboard and focus (including modals)
- [ ] Color/contrast and non-color status cues
- [ ] Loading, empty, error states
- [ ] PF6 components and project wrappers (`Select`, `ModalForm`)
- [ ] Tokens / layout components vs ad hoc CSS
- [ ] Copy and terminology consistent with MTV
- [ ] Matches closest existing plugin screen pattern

---

## Output format (review-phase)

```
🔴 A11Y ISSUE: [issue]
  WCAG: [guideline reference]
